## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | re-introduced | IMPORTANT | test/hub/hub_plugin_menu_flow_test.dart | ⚠️ important the interactive menu → stop wiring lost its only test — silently this pr converts the dap menu interactive host start pick test to the hermetic registerstarthost pipeline but deletes its sibling stop choice stops quietly when nothing is running 26 → 25 tests in the file — the only test count change in the whole pr the deletion is not mentioned in the pr description which only declares the start pick conversion hub menu tests the interactive start pick drives the same hermetic registerstarthost pipeline… it was the only test driving the interactive menu pick → dapstop wiring end to end the surviving not running assertions all cover the headless fa dap stop dispatch instead test hub dap command test dart 545 567 test cli fah hub serve dispatch test dart 124 test integration dap cli e2e test dart 182 hub plugin host test dart has no stop coverage at all if someone breaks the menu s stop action routing pick value action key handler call nothing fails the fix is cheap — the seam for a hermetic replacement already exists hubpluginhost takes hubstopper bin fah hub plugin dart 62 used at 1544 as hubstopper defaultstopper register with hubstopper async 0 plus the probe down defaults the start test uses pick stop assert the quiet line please restore it hermetically or state the intentional drop in the pr description |
| F2 | re-introduced | SUGGESTION | test/cli/agent_cli_test_support.dart | 💡 suggestion the doc comment s no stale waiter guarantee doesn t hold on the timeout path the comment promises firstwhere cancels its own subscription on completion so a stale waiter cannot linger on the broadcast stream after the await — that is true only when the needle matches when the timeout here fires the inner firstwhere future is orphaned its subscription stays attached to the chunks broadcast controller and the predicate buf tostring contains needle keeps re running on every later write until the io becomes unreachable cost is zero on green runs the throw already failed the test so this is contract wording plus failure path hygiene not a bug — but this helper is the pattern 1100 call sites now standardize on either soften the comment …on completion of the match or make the promise true keep the subscription and cancel it in ontimeout a streamiterator gives the same shape without a manual subscription |

### Candidates pending confirmation
- Round 2 finding "⚠️ important re raise — registry f1 still open at head c94765f8 the interactive menu → stop wiring still has no test — silently re raising the open finding from the previous round this pr converts the dap menu interactive host start pick test to the hermetic registerstarthost pipeline but deleted its sibling stop choice stops quietly when nothing is running the file went 26 → 25 tests — the only test count change in the whole pr and the deletion is not mentioned in the pr description which only declares the start pick conversion the new head the gh 2176 jdk sync does not touch this file — the finding stands unchanged it was the only test driving the interactive menu pick → dapstop wiring end to end the surviving not running assertions all cover the headless fa dap stop dispatch instead test hub dap command test dart 545 567 test cli fah hub serve dispatch test dart 124 test integration dap cli e2e test dart 182 hub plugin host test dart has no stop coverage at all if someone breaks the menu s stop action routing pick value action key handler call nothing fails the fix is cheap — the seam for a hermetic replacement already exists hubpluginhost takes hubstopper bin fah hub plugin dart 62 used at 1544 as hubstopper defaultstopper register with hubstopper async 0 plus the probe down defaults the start test uses pick stop assert the quiet line please restore it hermetically or state the intentional drop in the pr description" (test/hub/hub_plugin_menu_flow_test.dart:301) is possibly same as F1 — confirm ("same as F1") or mark it "new".

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

