## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | re-introduced | IMPORTANT | test/hub/hub_plugin_menu_flow_test.dart | ⚠️ important the interactive menu → stop wiring lost its only test — silently this pr converts the dap menu interactive host start pick test to the hermetic registerstarthost pipeline but deletes its sibling stop choice stops quietly when nothing is running 26 → 25 tests in the file — the only test count change in the whole pr the deletion is not mentioned in the pr description which only declares the start pick conversion hub menu tests the interactive start pick drives the same hermetic registerstarthost pipeline… it was the only test driving the interactive menu pick → dapstop wiring end to end the surviving not running assertions all cover the headless fa dap stop dispatch instead test hub dap command test dart 545 567 test cli fah hub serve dispatch test dart 124 test integration dap cli e2e test dart 182 hub plugin host test dart has no stop coverage at all if someone breaks the menu s stop action routing pick value action key handler call nothing fails the fix is cheap — the seam for a hermetic replacement already exists hubpluginhost takes hubstopper bin fah hub plugin dart 62 used at 1544 as hubstopper defaultstopper register with hubstopper async 0 plus the probe down defaults the start test uses pick stop assert the quiet line please restore it hermetically or state the intentional drop in the pr description |
| F2 | re-introduced | SUGGESTION | test/cli/agent_cli_test_support.dart | 💡 suggestion the doc comment s no stale waiter guarantee doesn t hold on the timeout path the comment promises firstwhere cancels its own subscription on completion so a stale waiter cannot linger on the broadcast stream after the await — that is true only when the needle matches when the timeout here fires the inner firstwhere future is orphaned its subscription stays attached to the chunks broadcast controller and the predicate buf tostring contains needle keeps re running on every later write until the io becomes unreachable cost is zero on green runs the throw already failed the test so this is contract wording plus failure path hygiene not a bug — but this helper is the pattern 1100 call sites now standardize on either soften the comment …on completion of the match or make the promise true keep the subscription and cancel it in ontimeout a streamiterator gives the same shape without a manual subscription |

### Candidates pending confirmation
- Round 3 finding "⚠️ important re raise — registry f1 confirmed same as f1 still open at head c3061bea the interactive menu → stop wiring still has no test — silently re raising the open finding for the third round this pr converts the dap menu interactive host start pick test to the hermetic registerstarthost pipeline but deleted its sibling stop choice stops quietly when nothing is running the file went 26 → 25 tests — the only test count change in the whole pr and the deletion is not mentioned in the pr description which only declares the start pick conversion neither later head touches this file the gh 2176 jdk sync nor the 2143 project mount sync — the finding stands unchanged it was the only test driving the interactive menu pick → dapstop wiring end to end the surviving not running assertions all cover the headless fa dap stop dispatch instead test hub dap command test dart 545 567 test cli fah hub serve dispatch test dart 124 test integration dap cli e2e test dart 182 hub plugin host test dart has no stop coverage at all if someone breaks the menu s stop action routing pick value action key handler call nothing fails the fix is cheap — the seam for a hermetic replacement already exists hubpluginhost takes hubstopper bin fah hub plugin dart 62 used at 1544 as hubstopper defaultstopper register with hubstopper async 0 plus the probe down defaults the start test uses pick stop assert the quiet line please restore it hermetically or state the intentional drop in the pr description" (test/hub/hub_plugin_menu_flow_test.dart:301) is possibly same as F1 — confirm ("same as F1") or mark it "new".

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

diff --git a/lib/src/cli/fa_tui_viewport.dart b/lib/src/cli/fa_tui_viewport.dart
index d6bad5e7b0..fe36b35a1c 100644
--- a/lib/src/cli/fa_tui_viewport.dart
+++ b/lib/src/cli/fa_tui_viewport.dart
@@ -234,7 +234,23 @@ extension _TuiViewport on FaTuiModel {
       // glass). The carried count = '\n's written before the anchor call
       // = the exact row the next write (the reconciliation summary)
       // lands on — the trailing phantom slot.
-      return (copyWith(bootAnchorLine: msg.line), null);
+      //
+      // The anchor landing re-runs the follow contract ONCE (issue
+      // #2172): every banner append happened BEFORE the anchor existed,
+      // so each one followed at the live edge — and when the wrapped
+      // banner alone overflows the viewport, that window sits past the
+      // banner's head ('[Model]' born above the fold). Nothing appends
+      // after the anchor on a fresh boot, so without this re-follow the
+      // wrong window would be the LAST word. With post-anchor content
+      // (a restored transcript) the replay's own appends re-follow
+      // anyway — same end state, one extra bounded pass.
+      final anchored = copyWith(bootAnchorLine: msg.line);
+      if (!followTail) return (anchored, null);
+      final wrapped = anchored._wrappedLines();
+      return (
+        anchored.copyWith(scrollOffset: anchored._followAnchor(wrapped)),
+        null,
+      );
     }

     if (msg is _SetInputTextMsg) {
@@ -278,12 +294,37 @@ extension _TuiViewport on FaTuiModel {
   /// '[Model]' never painted, every PTY suite timed out at waitForBoot).
   /// And when even the anchored region overflows, the tail outranks the
   /// boot region and the anchor degrades to the bottom.
+  ///
+  /// The park also needs CONTENT to park for (issue #2172): with an empty
+  /// post-anchor region — a FRESH boot whose banner alone overflows the
+  /// viewport (long temp-space workspace paths wrapping the [Context] and
+  /// [Session] rows past the transcript height) — `boot > bottom` holds
+  /// vacuously and the park showed a fully blank window while the whole
+  /// banner, [Model] block included, rode the fold: nothing repaints it,
+  /// so waitForBoot never saw the row. Parking is the replay tail's
+  /// privilege; with nothing after the anchor the window pins to the
+  /// banner's head instead, so the boot marker rows always paint.
   int _followAnchor(List<String> wrapped) {
     final bottom = _scrollBottom(wrapped);
     final boot = _bootAnchorRow();
     if (boot != null && wrapped.length > _viewportHeight) {
       final region = wrapped.length - boot;
-      if (region <= _viewportHeight && boot > bottom) return boot;
+      if (region > 1 && region <= _viewportHeight && boot > bottom) {
+        return boot;
+      }
+      if (region <= 1) {
+        // Fresh boot — nothing but the banner and the anchor's trailing
+        // phantom slot (issue #2172): pin the window to the banner's HEAD
+        // so the [Model] block paints even when the wrapped banner
+        // overflows the viewport (long temp-space workspace paths wrap
+        // the [Context]/[Session] rows past the transcript height). The
+        // live edge would pin to the bottom, and a head-born row like
+        // '[Model]' would never reach the glass; the banner's tail rides
+        // the fold instead. The pin dissolves on the first real
+        // post-anchor append (region > 1 resumes the park/bottom
+        // contract below).
+        return 0;
+      }
     }
     return bottom;
   }

diff --git a/test/cli/fa_tui_boot_banner_fold_test.dart b/test/cli/fa_tui_boot_banner_fold_test.dart
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..f0ee09714e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/cli/fa_tui_boot_banner_fold_test.dart
@@ -0,0 +1,103 @@
+// Issue #2172 regression: a fresh TUI boot whose banner alone overflows
+// the transcript viewport must still paint the banner's HEAD — the
+// '[Model]' block waitForBoot anchors on.
+//
+// The trigger shape: a workspace cwd long enough that the [Context] row
+// and the derived [Session] path wrap the boot banner past the viewport
+// height (macOS temp-space paths: /var/folders/…/T/fa_…_ws_XXXXXX wraps
+// where CI's short /tmp paths do not). Pre-fix the live-edge follow
+// pinned the first window to the bottom (and the boot anchor's trailing
+// phantom slot then parked it past the banner entirely) — the banner's
+// head was born above the fold, '[Model]' never reached the wire, and
+// every PTY waitForBoot timed out at 90 s on a chrome-only frame.
+//
+// Headless (issue #735 injected runner): the full AgentCli boots in-process,
+// frames are captured through TuiProgramHooks.output — no terminal involved.
+// 80x24 is the PTY harness default geometry.
+import 'dart:async';
+import 'dart:convert';
+import 'dart:typed_data';
+
+import 'package:flutter_agent_harness/flutter_agent_harness.dart';
+import 'package:flutter_agent_harness/src/cli/tui_repl.dart';
+import 'package:test/test.dart';
+
+import 'agent_cli_test_support.dart';
+
+class _FrameSink implements StreamConsumer<List<int>> {
+  final _bytes = BytesBuilder(copy: false);
+
+  void add(List<int> data) => _bytes.add(data);
+
+  void addError(Object error, [StackTrace? stackTrace]) {}
+
+  @override
+  Future<void> addStream(Stream<List<int>> stream) async {
+    await for (final chunk in stream) {
+      add(chunk);
+    }
+  }
+
+  @override
+  Future<void> close() async {}
+
+  String get text => utf8.decode(_bytes.toBytes(), allowMalformed: true);
+}
+
+void main() {
+  test('boot banner overflow: [Model] paints even when the banner wraps '
+      'past the viewport (#2172)', () async {
+    final frames = _FrameSink();
+    final keys = StreamController<List<int>>();
+    // A deep fake workspace path: the [Context] row wraps to several
+    // rows and the derived [Session] path wraps past it — together the
+    // banner exceeds the 80x24 transcript viewport (the #2172 shape).
+    final deepCwd =
+        '/${List.generate(10, (i) => 'segment-$i-longname').join('/')}';
+    final env = MemoryExecutionEnv(cwd: deepCwd);
+    final io = FakeCliIO();
+    final cli = AgentCli(
+      config: AgentCliConfig(
+        model: testModel,
+        apiKey: '[REDACTED:Sensitive-Value]',
+        env: env,
+        sessionRoot: '/sessions',
+        providerKind: 'openai-completions',
+        agentMode: 'code',
+        approvalMode: ApprovalMode.yolo,
+        skillsAccess: SkillsAccess.granted,
+        tuiClassic: true,
+        tuiProgramHooks: TuiProgramHooks(
+          input: keys.stream,
+          output: frames,
+          width: 80,
+          height: 24,
+        ),
+      ),
